# scripts/opcount: `hashbench bench N` writes one 4 KiB part N times to one
# sha256.Hasher (CAP-HASH); the cost of one write is the slope between the
# two sizes. 256 writes are the owner's 1 MiB in 4 KiB writes. The control
# is hand Go: the same part written N times to one sha256.New.
unit write
sizes 256 2560
args bench {n}
control benchmarks/hashstream/testdata/control
